{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Relation","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Iterate","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.light_cone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.light_cone","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L98-L116","doc":"The light cone.  If the synchronous update `F` reads, at particle `i`,\nonly the particles `adj`-joined to `i`, and two configurations differ only on\n`D`, then after `t` rounds they still agree at every particle not reached from\n`D` in `t` steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.Reach","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.Reach","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L92-L96","doc":"`Reach adj D t i`: particle `i` is joined to the set `D` by a path of\nexactly `t` steps of `adj` (with `adj` reflexive this is \"within `t` steps\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.isProduct_of_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.isProduct_of_stable","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L79-L84","doc":"A stable start state is its own only product: nothing moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.exists_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.exists_product","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L74-L77","doc":"Every start state has at least one product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.IsProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.IsProduct","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L68-L72","doc":"A product of a start state: a stable state reachable from it by improving\nmoves.  Two distinct products of the same start are two outcomes of the same\nreactants along different pathways (the cascade's isomers). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.no_infinite_cascade","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.no_infinite_cascade","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L61-L66","doc":"No cascade of improving moves is infinite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.potential_drop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.potential_drop","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L53-L59","doc":"Along any cascade, after `k` moves the potential has dropped by at least `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.exists_stable_of_potential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.exists_stable_of_potential","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L34-L51","doc":"Every state reaches a stable state by improving moves, if every move\nstrictly lowers a natural-number potential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.Stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.ChainReaction.Stable","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/ChainReaction.lean#L31-L32","doc":"A state is stable when no improving move leaves it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}